# Push gate: fast-forward main with a clean secret scan, annotated v* tags, and bounded ref input.
# The bundled gate owns the policy; backups and lane refs use the same policy as the runtime. Then the harness refuses a
# committed @starci pin npm cannot install, or a local package copy ahead of npm (starci deps check). Last, every push carries the warm check
# cache a real run on its tree writes, so CI re-checks only the diff: `app check --fresh` refuses a cache that run had to change
# (HFS_CHECK_CACHE_UNWARMED) and a host that cannot write a portable one (HFS_CHECK_CACHE_UNPORTABLE).
set -e
node --input-type=module -e "import { main } from '@starci/hfs/runtime/scripts/guards/release-push-gate.mjs'; process.exit(await main());"
node node_modules/starci-harness/dist/main.js deps check
node node_modules/starci-harness/dist/main.js app check --fresh
